[0.003, "o", "Usage: chroot [OPTION]... NEWROOT [COMMAND [ARG]...]\r\nRun COMMAND with root directory set to NEWROOT.\r\n\r\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#chroot--groups\u001b\\\u001b[1m--groups=G_LIST\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\r\n         specify supplementary groups as g1,g2,..,gN\r\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#chroot--userspec\u001b\\\u001b[1m--userspec=USER:GROUP\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\r\n         specify user and group (ID or name) to use\r\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#chroot--skip-chdir\u001b\\\u001b[1m--skip-chdir\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\r\n         do not change working directory to '/'\r\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/chroot#chroot--help\u001b\\\u001b[1m--help\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\r\n         display this help and exit\r\n      \u001b]8;;https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/chroot#chroot--version\u001b\\\u001b[1m--version\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\\r\n         output version information and exit\r\n\r\nIf no command is given, run '\"$SHELL\" -i' (default: '/bin/sh -i').\r\n\r\nExit status:\r\n  125  if the chroot command itself fails\r\n  126  if COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked\r\n  127  if COMMAND cannot be found\r\n  -    the exit status of COMMAND otherwise\r\n\r\nReport bugs to: bug-coreutils@gnu.org\r\nGNU coreutils home page: <https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/>\r\nGeneral help using GNU software: <https://www.gnu.org/gethelp/>\r\nReport any translation bugs to <https://translationproject.org/team/>\r\nFull documentation <https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/chroot>\r\nor available locally via: info '(coreutils) chroot invocation'\r\n"]
